- Story & Context: In the dusty town of Ocotillo, a stray shard of nickel-iron pierced the soil, causing the local flora to hum with electrical current for three days. Mireya touched the glowing sap, inadvertently synchronizing her own heartbeat to the erratic rhythms of the encroaching space-matter. As the greenhouse lights flickered in binary, she realized the land was no longer just dirt, but a giant, buried machine. "Roots bite deeper when the sky feeds the soil."
