Track 2: Venga el Engranaje
- Story & Context: Standing at the edge of the great glass conservatory, old Mateo confesssed to the village elders that he had been replacing his accordion’s reeds with filings from the crater for a decade. He explained the guilt of the sound, how the music started to dream without him, creating a life of its own in the gears. He clutched his instrument, the cold metal burning his palms as he played for mercy. "The iron knows the secrets I buried in the dust."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An elderly, weathered musician holding an accordion that is visibly vibrating, releasing small, glowing sparks and tiny, translucent clockwork butterflies into a dimly lit, circular room.

Track 3: Greenhouse Epiphany
- Story & Context: The final bloom occurred during the solstice, as the garden erupted into a symphony of ticking, metallic petals that signaled the end of the harvest. Everyone who attended the performance at the Great Conservatory felt their temporal awareness fracture, realizing the meteorites weren't falling, but returning home. The music stopped abruptly, leaving only the sound of thousands of tiny gears clicking into a permanent, frozen state of perfection. "Time stops when the flowers learn to speak."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An overgrown, abandoned greenhouse overflowing with metallic, mechanical flowers reaching toward a fractured, swirling sky; high contrast, surrealist, epic scale.

